---
// Privacy and cookie notice. Plain, first person, and only what actually happens: the enquiry form
// and its confirmation email (worker/enquiry.js), analytics only after Accept (ConsentBanner.astro),
// hosting, and the client documents on docs.anthonyis.uk (worker/docs: signing record, signing cookie).
// Suppliers are described by what they do, never by name (Anthony, 14 November 2026), so the page
// doesn't need changing when a supplier does. Cookies are listed by purpose for the same reason.
// 29 October 2026, details confirmed 2 November 2026. No ICO fee: exempt (self-assessment, 2 November 2026).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Schema from '../../components/Schema.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { URLS, ENTITY } from '../../data/site';

const P = {
  path: URLS.privacy,
  title: 'Privacy and Cookies | Anthony is Freelance',
  description: 'How Anthony is Freelance handles your details: what the enquiry form collects, the analytics cookies used only if you accept, and your rights.',
  eyebrow: 'Privacy and cookies',
  heading: 'What I collect, why, and what you can ask for.',
  intro: 'This site collects very little. The enquiry form sends me what you type, and analytics only run if you accept cookies.',
  updated: { iso: '2026-11-14', label: '14 November 2026' },
};
const { business } = ENTITY;
const mail = `mailto:${business.email}`;
---
<Base title={P.title} description={P.description}>
  <Schema
    slot="head"
    title={P.title}
    description={P.description}
    path={P.path}
    about={ENTITY.business.id}
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: URLS.home }, { name: 'Privacy and cookies', path: P.path }]}
  />
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <PageHero eyebrow={P.eyebrow} heading={P.heading} intro={P.intro}>
      <p class="t-label tracking-[0.02em] text-muted">Updated <time datetime={P.updated.iso}>{P.updated.label}</time></p>
    </PageHero>

    <section class="px-margin py-section">
      <div class="prose-article lg:w-half">
        <h2>Who I am</h2>
        <p>
          This site belongs to {business.legalName}, trading as {business.name}, registered in England and Wales
          (company number {business.companyNumber}), with its registered office at {business.registeredOffice}. I'm based
          in {business.locality}, {business.region}. I'm Anthony Bliss,
          the director, and I decide how your details are used. You can reach me at <a href={mail}>{business.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>The enquiry form</h2>
        <p>
          When you send the form, I receive your name, email, website, budget, message and how you found me. I use them to
          reply to you and, if we work together, to run the project. Nothing goes on a mailing list, and I never sell or share
          it for marketing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The form reaches my inbox through an email delivery service, which also sends you a short confirmation. If you
          email me directly, the same applies.
        </p>
        <p>
          I keep enquiries that don't become projects for two years, then delete them. Client records are kept for
          six years, because UK company and tax law requires it.
        </p>

        <h2>Quotes, contracts and invoices</h2>
        <p>
          If we work together, your quote, contract and invoices sit on private pages that only you and I have the links
          to. I can see when a document was first opened. When you sign a contract online, I keep a record of who signed
          and when, including the email address the signing code went to, your IP address and your browser, as proof of
          the signature.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Analytics cookies only load if you press Accept on the cookie banner. They tell me which pages people visit, how
          they found the site and what device they used, so I can improve it. The analytics don't give me your name or
          contact details.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>What it does</th><th>How long</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Your cookie choice (browser storage, not a cookie)</td><td>Remembers whether you accepted or rejected analytics</td><td>Six months</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Analytics cookies</td><td>Tell visits apart. Only set after Accept</td><td>Up to two years</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Security cookie</td><td>Stops automated attacks. Needed for the site to work safely</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Signing cookie</td><td>Checks the code emailed to you when you sign a contract online. Needed for signing to work</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          You can change your mind any time with Cookie settings at the bottom of every page. Analytics data is kept for
          14 months, then deleted automatically.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else handles your details</h2>
        <p>I use a small number of suppliers to run the site and the business:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Website hosting and security.</li>
          <li>Email delivery, for the enquiry form and the codes used to sign contracts.</li>
          <li>Email and file storage, for my inbox and client documents.</li>
          <li>Analytics, only if you accept.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you'd like to know who they are, ask and I'll tell you. Some of them store data outside the UK. When they do,
          they use the safeguards UK data protection law approves.
        </p>

        <h2>Why I'm allowed to use it</h2>
        <p>
          Replying to an enquiry and running a project are steps towards, or part of, a contract with you. Analytics rely on
          your consent, which you can withdraw. Keeping client records rests on a legal obligation, and the signing record on
          my legitimate interest in being able to show a contract was signed.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask me for a copy of your details, ask me to correct or delete them, object to how I use them, or ask me to
          stop. Email <a href={mail}>{business.email}</a> and I'll reply within one month.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you're unhappy with how I've handled your details, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at{' '}
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113. I'd appreciate the chance to put
          it right first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
